      "timestamp": "2026-09-25T11:58:12.574256Z",
      "user_text": "For the Ising model $H=-J\\sum_{\\langle ij\\rangle}s_is_j$ ($s=\\pm\\frac12$), find the infinite-temperature energy moments $\\langle H^2\\rangle,\\langle H^3\\rangle$ without specifying a lattice shape, as a general formula in graph invariants (edge count $|E|$, triangle count $N_\\triangle$). For the Ising model, $\\langle H^3\\rangle$ is proportional to the triangle count $N_\\triangle$ alone.",
      "visible_action": "Memo",
      "operation": null,
      "operation_args": {},
